    1	"""
    2	Cross-x amortisation, slot 3 of Thread 5: HKM / Lucy DP / Meissel-Lehmer
    3	combinatorial pillar.
    4	
    5	Builds an instrumented batched Lucy DP that decouples shared state from
    6	per-x state.
    7	
    8	Decomposition:
    9	  shared state  := small[v] for v <= sqrt(x_max), and the prime list.
    10	                   Equivalently, sieve of Eratosthenes up to sqrt(x_max).
    11	  per-x state   := large_i[v] for v <= sqrt(x_i), one array per query.
    12	
    13	Lucy DP cost decomposition (BASIC, no Fenwick — focus on structural shape,
    14	not the log factor):
    15	
    16	  T_setup_shared(x_max) = O(sqrt(x_max) log log x_max)
    17	                          [sieve of Eratosthenes up to sqrt(x_max)]
    18	  T_per_x_evaluation(x_i) = O(x_i / log x_i)
    19	                          [large[] sweep over primes p <= sqrt(x_i)]
    20	
    21	  T_total(M, x_max, x_avg) = T_setup_shared(x_max) + M * T_per_x(x_avg)
    22	  T_per_x_amortised(M)     = T_setup_shared(x_max) / M + T_per_x(x_avg)
    23	
